<title>FRANCE: French November unemployment rises by 20,700.</title>
<headline>French November unemployment rises by 20,700.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The seasonally adjusted number of people unemployed in France in November rose by 20,700, or 0.7 percent, to 3,121,500, Labour Ministry data showed.</p>
<p>The jobless rate, based on International Labour Organisation (ILO) criteria, which excludes jobseekers who did any work, increased to a fresh record of 12.7 percent, in line with economists' forecasts.  </p>
<p>The ministry gave the following seasonally adjusted data:</p>
<p>				  end-Nov   month-on-month year-on-year</p>
<p> Jobless rate (ILO)	 12.7 pct  +0.1 pctge pt  +1.1 pctge pt</p>
<p> Unemployment		3,121,500    +0.7 pct	   +5.0 pct</p>
<p> Unemployment (ILO)	3,257,000    +0.5 pct	  +10.7 pct</p>
<p> Jobs offered		  198,600   +16.3 pct	   +6.1 pct</p>
<p> New jobless registrations 355,600    -5.6 pct	   -5.7 pct</p>
<p> Jobless register exits    351,700    -0.5 pct</p>
<p> Men under 25		  292,500    +0.6 pct	  +6.2 pct</p>
<p> Women under 25		331,700    +0.4 pct	  +2.2 pct</p>
<p> Men between 25 and 49   1,051,400    +1.0 pct	  +6.5 pct</p>
<p> Women between 25 and 49 1,070,000    +0.4 pct	  +2.9 pct</p>
<p> Men 50 and over	     215,700    +0.9 pct	  +8.3 pct</p>
<p> Women 50 and over	   160,200    +0.5 pct	  +8.7 pct</p>
<p> Redundancy		     27,200    -4.6 pct	   0.0 pct</p>
<p> Jobless for over 12 mos 1,084,600    +2.1 pct	  +3.0 pct</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
